    "title": "Utica's 4th of July fireworks celebration new location - NewsBreak",
    "text": "6 hours ago UTICA, N.Y. (WFXV/WUTR) – Starting with America’s 250th, Utica’s annual Independence Day fireworks celebration will have a new location. In June, the City of Utica announced the event will be be moved from its usual venue of Thomas R. Proctor Park to Harbor Point on the city’s north side. Mayor Michael Galime says the decision was made to address safety concerns as well as draw people to the downtown area. Read full article\n1",
